Forgot to add;

Your AGFA plates are more than likely stilll fine for holography. The big nine metre hologram I did last year at the Holocenter was on old Agfa film. And at home I still use Ilford film which is over 18 years old and works fine. Today I am more skeptical about Slavich film. The thing I hate about this film is that you must almost immediately process it otherwise the latent image will begin to fade. I did tests years ago wanting to expose a 10metre x 10cm roll of PGF -03 film in sections over time then process it about a week later. Tests showed that the film I had exposed a day earlier had almost no image after processing compared to the half that I had cut off after exposure and processed immediately. The latent image does not fade with Agfa/Ilford film. How I long for the days of Agfa film/plates.

